<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Johnson returns two weeks after starting sertraline 50 mg and is seen the same day by Dr. Hassan of neurology. He has taken it every morning. He had mild nausea for the first four days, which has passed, and no agitation or sleep change. His mood is no better yet; he still cannot write and has seen only one friend. The nurse called him after the first week, and he has had two psychotherapy sessions. He told Dr. Hassan about the movements and sounds he has made since boyhood, the urge he feels before each one, his habit of counting his steps at doorways and going back to start again if he gets it wrong, and his fear that all of this, with his low spirits, means he is going mad. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sertraline</td><td>50 mg daily for two weeks, every dose taken</td></tr><tr><td>Side effects</td><td>Nausea for four days, resolved</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 19</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>Two sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Tics</td><td>Lifelong; urge before each; rituals at doorways</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
